From 12a036ad5189bb8ddde5918a620634d9aadf52e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:29:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] build(windows): build-windows.cmd with llvm-mingw, SQLite
 compiled in, the UTF-8 manifest; tests/c1_acceptance.py; 0.3.2

- build-windows.cmd: libspklib.a, spklib-host.exe and spklib-tests.exe with
  clang, llvm-ar and llvm-windres from llvm-mingw (LLVM_MINGW or PATH), as
  build.sh is on a Mac: no CMake, no package manager. Static (-static), so
  the helper is one file. `test` runs the tests with TMP and TEMP inside
  build\windows-x64\tmp. `release` is optimised, stripped and written
  without a timestamp (--no-insert-timestamp, -ffile-prefix-map), so the
  same sources and toolchain give the same bytes; it writes the .sha256.
- third_party/sqlite/fetch.py: SQLite 3.54.1's amalgamation, checked
  against the size and SHA3-256 sqlite.org publishes before it is unpacked;
  the three files are not committed. macOS keeps the system SQLite.
- host/spklib.manifest (+ spklib.rc): activeCodePage UTF-8 and
  longPathAware, embedded in the host and the tests.
- tests/c1_acceptance.py: drives spklib-host over stdio against a real
  Capture One catalog (and session) and checks every answer against an
  independent reading of a byte copy of the database, plus a size / mtime /
  SHA-256 census of every file before and after. Standard library only;
  runs on macOS too.
- .gitattributes: *.cmd with CRLF (cmd.exe needs it for labels).
- VERSION 0.3.2: the Windows port. abi 1 and schema 3 unchanged.

Gate: tests/c1_acceptance.py on Linux against a synthetic catalog and
session (non-ASCII names, ZPARENT -1, an in-package location) -- 31 passed,
0 failed. build-windows.cmd is first run on the Windows PC.

